                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "e99d4493-84c0-316d-8d2c-3e06f43d426b",
                        "entry_id": "104f230c-329c-3155-b602-ca126c6ef70e",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Foamy; having a large head."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "of a drink"
                        ],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "a6f917d4-a8ce-3b00-8767-25099823c3ed",
                        "entry_id": "104f230c-329c-3155-b602-ca126c6ef70e",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Nervous, excitable."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "of a horse"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "b1843dc7-ff49-4dc2-8e5d-f1661906c5ec",
                                "sense_id": "a6f917d4-a8ce-3b00-8767-25099823c3ed",
                                "text": "‘He's a mutton-fisted beggar; but the horse is a bit nappy, and young Roger'll be the man to keep him going at his fences.’"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "1ff84300-85af-4593-822c-18fb19daca88",
                                "sense_id": "a6f917d4-a8ce-3b00-8767-25099823c3ed",
                                "text": "I do feel, however, that in talking lightheartedly of making rearing, pulling or nappy horses into useful members of equine society I am treading on very dangerous ground."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "14c5da7a-c771-4683-a352-a425451e5970",
                                "sense_id": "a6f917d4-a8ce-3b00-8767-25099823c3ed",
                                "text": "Note that it is possible that a horse is not in fact being nappy at all, but is suffering the onset of muscle disorders: it is up to the rider to interpret the signs correctly."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "0f1f3b95-6848-4308-82e4-f17674ef455f",
                                "sense_id": "a6f917d4-a8ce-3b00-8767-25099823c3ed",
                                "text": "When riders are too dominant various problems can arise: a horse may become nappy, or refuse to go forward."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [],
                "word_linkages": []
            },
            {
                "entry_id": "ca8e7aa9-0f3e-3c41-894b-5e8ed8668cb6",
                "word": "nappy",
                "pos": "adj",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
