            {
                "entry_id": "ab1a24a7-bf6f-3aee-98d9-ba93cce40396",
                "word": "nappy",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "08963760-eb59-49b9-90ae-abd740df5b51",
                        "entry_id": "ab1a24a7-bf6f-3aee-98d9-ba93cce40396",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "nappies"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "6eb5c5ff-e814-3c13-a6eb-28c6fb46b64e",
                        "entry_id": "ab1a24a7-bf6f-3aee-98d9-ba93cce40396",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A shallow, flat-bottomed earthenware or glass bowl with sloping sides."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "1d97de54-7a0f-43c5-a6c2-3adc2483da2a",
                                "sense_id": "6eb5c5ff-e814-3c13-a6eb-28c6fb46b64e",
                                "text": "Suppose you advertise a “five-inch glass nappy.” It doesn′t tell a reader anything — a woman especially. She can′t tell how big five inches are anyway ; but just say, “large imitation cut glass fruit saucers at thirty cents a dozen,” and get your packers ready."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "bd4d8efc-9806-4642-9504-7920339d37b6",
                                "sense_id": "6eb5c5ff-e814-3c13-a6eb-28c6fb46b64e",
                                "text": "The use of a glazed earthenware nesting-dish, or “nappy, ” 9 inches in diameter across the top, is strongly advised."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "61411b66-55e8-4fa5-a32a-d62029d3f9c7",
                                "sense_id": "6eb5c5ff-e814-3c13-a6eb-28c6fb46b64e",
                                "text": "Place a slice of pineapple in a fruit nappy, place on it a No. 10 cone of vanilla ice cream and pour over it a ladle of chop suey dressing, crowning it with a freshly opened lycher nut or a cherry."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [],
                "word_linkages": []
            },
            {
                "entry_id": "a5fe8d12-95d9-358d-9570-ab2f19e58424",
                "word": "nappy",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "02e6ff22-4ac1-4c42-bc11-f48881a3f242",
                        "entry_id": "a5fe8d12-95d9-358d-9570-ab2f19e58424",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "nappies"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "58b96466-6ee6-3a8e-bb40-2aef04e8cb63",
                        "entry_id": "a5fe8d12-95d9-358d-9570-ab2f19e58424",
                        "glosses": [
                            "An absorbent garment worn by a baby or toddler who does not yet have voluntary control of their bladder and bowels or by someone who is incontinent; a diaper."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Australia",
                            "British",
                            "Ireland",
                            "New-Zealand",
                            "South-Africa"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "65e35984-83cd-47b7-95c5-c88722f5b166",
                                "sense_id": "58b96466-6ee6-3a8e-bb40-2aef04e8cb63",
                                "text": "You will notice that disposable nappies are sold in boy and girl versions. They vary in where the thickest padding is provided."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b5dfaadf-e441-47c2-b5db-0908d793fc69",
                                "sense_id": "58b96466-6ee6-3a8e-bb40-2aef04e8cb63",
                                "text": "Other equipment required was soap for hand washing and washing of nappies, a washing line for the drying of nappies,[…]."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "8205bd97-33fe-4a9d-9aa3-5f93fd625c2f",
                                "sense_id": "58b96466-6ee6-3a8e-bb40-2aef04e8cb63",
                                "text": "You could burn disposable nappies (not a very practical option); otherwise, it′s probably best to take a supply of large plastic bags or nappy sacks with you and to dispose of them as thoughtfully as you can."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "428f9e27-51d3-4761-a140-564b75b47541",
                                "sense_id": "58b96466-6ee6-3a8e-bb40-2aef04e8cb63",
                                "text": "In response we mailed hundreds of nappies to students in halls. On the nappy was a simple message, IT'S A LOT EASIER TO PUT ON A CONDOM."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [],
                "word_linkages": [
                    {
                        "linkage_id": "8cd1b641-c946-4f49-9446-986df949beb9",
                        "source_entry_id": "a5fe8d12-95d9-358d-9570-ab2f19e58424",
                        "source_sense_ids": [
                            "58b96466-6ee6-3a8e-bb40-2aef04e8cb63"
                        ],
                        "linkage_type": "synonyms",
